From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 11:30:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] media: meson: vdec: vp9: an interrupt without a parsed header
 is no error

The microcode also interrupts with no header parsed: dec_status 0, as
for its debug messages through DEBUG_REG1, which Amlogic's driver
clears. The driver took every such interrupt for a fault and aborted.
With CMA full of movable pages, the first 4K decode's CAPTURE buffers
took a second to migrate in, and the session aborted on one of these.

Ignore an interrupt without a parsed header, as Amlogic's driver does,
and clear the debug tag.
---
 vdec/codec_vp9.c | 8 +++++---
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/vdec/codec_vp9.c b/vdec/codec_vp9.c
index 180ad8c..86d1d70 100644
--- a/vdec/codec_vp9.c
+++ b/vdec/codec_vp9.c
@@ -20,6 +20,8 @@
 #define VP9_RPM_BUFFER		HEVC_ASSIST_SCRATCH_1
 #define VP9_SHORT_TERM_RPS	HEVC_ASSIST_SCRATCH_2
 #define VP9_ADAPT_PROB_REG	HEVC_ASSIST_SCRATCH_3
+/* the microcode's debug tag, which it also interrupts for */
+#define VP9_DEBUG_REG		HEVC_ASSIST_SCRATCH_G
 #define VP9_MMU_MAP_BUFFER	HEVC_ASSIST_SCRATCH_4
 #define VP9_PPS_BUFFER		HEVC_ASSIST_SCRATCH_5
 #define VP9_SAO_UP		HEVC_ASSIST_SCRATCH_6
@@ -2225,9 +2227,9 @@ static irqreturn_t codec_vp9_threaded_isr(struct amvdec_session *sess)
 
 	mutex_lock(&vp9->lock);
 	if (dec_status != VP9_HEAD_PARSER_DONE) {
-		dev_err(core->dev_dec, "Unrecognized dec_status: %08X\n",
-			dec_status);
-		amvdec_abort(sess);
+		dev_dbg(core->dev_dec, "dec_status %08X, debug tag %08X: no header, ignored\n",
+			dec_status, amvdec_read_dos(core, VP9_DEBUG_REG));
+		amvdec_write_dos(core, VP9_DEBUG_REG, 0);
 		goto unlock;
 	}
 
-- 
